# Authority follows interaction, the host first: the guest throws the ball into the pile and the
# host's heroine walks into the same pile while it still moves. The bodies the guest set going are
# the guest's until her character touches them; then the host takes them back and the guest's
# copies are pulled to the host's (the second layer's correction for the loser).
scenario authority_host_push
scene pile60
seed 61
guests 1
end 14s
light_mass 20kg
authority interaction

net g1 rtt 100ms jitter 20ms loss 2%

p1 grab ball as grab
p1 wait 300ms
p1 throw pile31 speed 12 as throw
at 600ms p0 walk 3.4 -0.2 speed 3 as host_push

expect result grab granted
expect result throw done
expect result host_push done
expect agree_at_rest 1cm 2deg
expect no_stuck
# Derived: a body this guest simulates is moved by the seam only at a take, which keeps its pose
# (README "Authority follows interaction"): nothing but float noise, 1 cm.
expect local_correction.max <= 1cm
# Derived: the same correction of its turn. The stand reads an angle through acosf of a float
# dot product, 2 sqrt(2 n 2^-24) rad for a dot n ulps off 1: 0.04 deg a ulp, 0.16 deg at 16,
# which three float products of unit turns stay within; the least turn a placement shows is a
# hundredth of a radian, 0.57 deg: 0.25 deg.
expect local_turn.max <= 0.25deg
# Derived as in layer_pile: a render offset's release, 0.15 of at most 2 m.
expect jump.max <= 0.3m
# Measured 58 takes, 4 bodies taken back by the host's heroine and 56 returns at rest (seed 61);
# the bounds say each rule ran at all.
expect takes.count >= 20
expect reclaims.count >= 1
expect returns.count >= 20
# Derived: between two take-backs a prediction's pull is paused at most (120 + 60) / 2 of any
# 120 ticks (sync_soft.h: the chain cap 60, drained a tick per tick without a touch): 90.
expect pause_window.max <= 90t
